t":172,"end":172,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":173,"end":173,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Motif","start":231,"end":238,"description":"Nuclear localization signal 2"},{"type":"Domain","start":236,"end":496,"description":"Deacetylase sirtuin-type"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":238,"end":238,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Region","start":256,"end":259,"description":"Required for interaction with the sumoylated form of CCAR2"},{"type":"Binding site","start":261,"end":280,"description":"NAD(+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":345,"end":348,"description":"NAD(+)"},{"type":"Active site","start":363,"end":363,"description":"Proton acceptor"},{"type":"Binding site","start":371,"end":371,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":374,"end":374,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":377,"end":377,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Binding site","start":395,"end":395,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":395,"end":395,"description":"S-nitrosocysteine"},{"type":"Binding site","start":398,"end":398,"description":"Zn(2+)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":398,"end":398,"description":"S-nitrosocysteine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":430,"end":430,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Motif","start":433,"end":439,"description":"Nuclear export signal 2"},{"type":"Binding site","start":440,"end":442,"description":"NAD(+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":465,"end":467,"description":"NAD(+)"},{"type":"Binding site","start":482,"end":482,"description":"NAD(+)"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":513,"end":513,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":530,"end":530,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by DYRK1A, DYRK3 and MAPK8"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":535,"end":535,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Region","start":538,"end":540,"description":"Phosphorylated at one of three serine residues"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":544,"end":544,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":545,"end":545,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":610,"end":610,"description":"N6-acetyllysine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":659,"end":659,"description":"Phosphoserine; by CaMK2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":661,"end":661,"description":"Phosphoserine; by CaMK2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":719,"end":719,"description":"Phosphothreonine"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":747,"end":747,"description":"Phosphoserine"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts with XBP1 isoform 2 (PubMed:20955178). Found in a complex with PCAF and MYOD1. Interacts with FOXO1; the interaction deacetylates FOXO1, resulting in its nuclear retention and promotion of its transcriptional activity Component of the eNoSC complex, composed of SIRT1, SUV39H1 and RRP8. Interacts with HES1, HEY2 and PML. Interacts with RPS19BP1/AROS. Interacts with CCAR2 (via N-terminus); the interaction disrupts the interaction between SIRT1 and p53/TP53. Interacts with SETD7; the interaction induces the dissociation of SIRT1 from p53/TP53 and increases p53/TP53 activity. Interacts with MYCN, NR1I2, CREBZF, TSC2, TLE1, FOS, JUN, NR0B2, PPARG, NCOR, IRS1, IRS2 and NMNAT1. Interacts with HNF1A; the interaction occurs under nutrient restriction. Interacts with SUZ12; the interaction mediates the association with the PRC4 histone methylation complex which is specific as an association with PCR2 and PCR3 complex variants is not found. Interacts with BCL6; leads to a epigenetic repression of specific target genes. Interacts with CLOCK, BMAL1 and PER2 (By similarity). Interacts with PPARA; the interaction seems to be modulated by NAD(+) levels (PubMed:24043310). Interacts with NR1H3 and this interaction is inhibited in the presence of CCAR2. Interacts with CHEK2. Interacts with p53/TP53. Exhibits a preferential interaction with sumoylated CCAR2 over its unmodified form. Interacts with PACS2 (PubMed:29656858). Interacts with SIRT7 (By similarity). Interacts with PUS7 (PubMed:31451225). Interacts with TULP3 (PubMed:35397207). Interacts with MORN3; the interaction enhances the ubiquitination of p53/TP53 (PubMed:29681526). Interacts with NAP1L2; to promote deacetylation of histone H3 on 'Lys-14' (PubMed:35032339). Interacts with NOC4L (via C-terminus); the interaction results in inhibition of SIRT1-mediated deacetylation of TP53/p53 (PubMed:36030331)"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"(Microbial infection) Interacts with HIV-1 Tat"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q96EB6-2","name":"2","synonyms":["delta-exon8"],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Deacetylates 'Lys-382' of p53/TP53, however with lower activity than isoform 1. In combination, the two isoforms exert an additive effect. Isoform 2 regulates p53/TP53 expression and cellular stress response and is in turn repressed by p53/TP53 presenting a SIRT1 isoform-dependent auto-regulatory loop"}],"length":561,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000923647.1"],"refseq":[],"refseqProteins":[],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,453],[454,640,108]],"edits":[{"start":454,"end":639,"original":"SIPHEVPQILINREPLPHLHFDVELLGDCDVIINELCHRL","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":186,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":72,"foldedMissing":72,"features":[[3,80,0],[9,88,0],[16,43,0],[32,3,0],[33,1,0],[34,1,0],[35,1,0],[36,1,0],[37,3,0],[38,1,0],[39,1,0],[40,1,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q96EB6-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q96EB6-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":63.2,"plddt":[[0,27],[50,1],[0,48],[50,6],[0,1],[50,1],[0,61],[50,4],[70,5],[50,2],[0,17],[50,5],[70,8],[90,2],[70,2],[90,2],[70,1],[90,11],[70,11],[90,2],[70,2],[90,2],[70,2],[90,1],[70,9],[50,1],[70,12],[90,1],[70,1],[90,13],[70,1],[90,4],[70,1],[90,1],[70,30],[90,12],[70,2],[90,1],[70,7],[90,59],[70,1],[90,33],[70,2],[90,1],[70,2],[90,4],[70,1],[90,2],[70,11],[90,3],[70,12],[5